# Test suite, operator tooling, and fixtures aren't needed by the running
# service -- Dockerfile only ever `uv sync`/runs the package itself. See
# ISSUES.md's now-closed "Docker images ship the test suite, scripts, and
# fixtures with no .dockerignore" Parked Issue.
**/tests/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Operator CLI tooling and demo/test fixtures never used at runtime by the
# deployed service.
scripts/
fixtures/
SPEC.md
cost.md

# Never let a build context pick up local secrets or machine-specific config
# even though .dockerignore is a second, redundant safety net alongside
# .gitignore and the git-tracked-files-only build context most CI setups use.
.env
**/.env
.env.config
**/.env.config
*.pem
# Any service-account / private-key JSON, whatever it happens to be named.
# `gcp-service-account-key*.json` alone silently failed to match the real
# on-disk `vertex-ai-private-key.json`, so a local `docker build .` (which
# the deploy-verify skill runs) swept a live GCP service-account key into the
# build context. The explicit name stays below the glob for documentation.
*private-key*.json
*service-account*.json
gcp-service-account-key*.json

.git/
.venv/
docs/superpowers/
